# Deploy your workloads

## Create a sprint plan

Your sprint plan breaks down your primary migration plan into smaller, executable sprints. This involves grouping workloads into logical "waves" based on their dependencies, business priority, or complexity. This plan defines the what, when, and how for each wave, creating a clear roadmap for your team to follow

## Deploy your first migration wave

Now it's time for action. In this step, you'll deploy the initial group of workloads into their new cloud environment. Treat this first wave as a valuable learning experience. Be prepared to resolve any unexpected issues and use the insights you gain to refine your process for all subsequent waves


