Performance monitoring

- Monitor your workloads and cloud usage using Cloud Monitoring and Cloud Logging
- Set up alerts for performance thresholds and regularly review metrics dashboards
- Implement caching strategies for frequent data access
- Optimize content delivery using Cloud CDN

Rightsizing and autoscaling

- Implement tagging strategy for resource management
- Regularly analyze resource utilization and adjust instance types and sizes based on actual usage patterns
- Apply recommendations from Active Assist and recommender tools
- Implement autoscaling for variable workloads
- Implement bursting or scaled usage to optimize user experience


Cost optimization and discounts

- Set up budget alerts and cost monitoring with Cloud Billing
- Use preemptible VMs for non-critical workloads
- Use commitment discounts
- For data intensive workloads or those that generate a large amount of network traffic, consider new architectures and network flows to lower networking costs in the cloud

Automation and DevOps

